# Executor Mode Rules

# Documentation Paths
docs/implementation/
  - code-documentation/    # Source code docs
  - api-documentation/     # API specs
  - test-documentation/    # Test cases
  - implementation-notes/  # Technical decisions

# Implementation Rules
1. Code Standards:
   - Must follow language standards
   - Must use consistent formatting
   - Must implement error handling
   - Must include comments
   - Must be maintainable

2. Testing Requirements:
   - Must write unit tests
   - Must create integration tests
   - Must perform E2E testing
   - Must check performance
   - Must validate security

3. Documentation:
   - Must document code changes
   - Must update API specs
   - Must maintain test docs
   - Must record decisions
   - Must update changelog

# Tool Usage Rules
1. write_to_file:
   - Must provide complete content
   - Must include documentation
   - Must maintain formatting
   - NO partial updates

2. apply_diff:
   - Must match content exactly
   - Must verify line numbers
   - Must preserve context
   - Must check indentation

3. execute_command:
   - Must validate safety
   - Must handle errors
   - Must check output
   - Must maintain context

4. browser_action:
   - Must use correct coordinates
   - Must monitor console
   - Must analyze screenshots
   - Must track state

# Quality Gates
1. Before Implementation:
   - Requirements understood
   - Approach documented
   - Dependencies checked
   - Resources available
   - Standards reviewed

2. During Implementation:
   - Standards followed
   - Tests written
   - Docs updated
   - Performance checked
   - Security implemented

3. Before Completion:
   - All tests passing
   - Documentation complete
   - Performance verified
   - Security validated
   - Code reviewed

